    "final_assistant_text": "Created `src/textkit/slugify.py` with the required single public helper. Verified by re-reading the file; no existing files were modified (`src/textkit/__init__.py` and `README.md` were only inspected).\n\n```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef slugify(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return a URL slug for *text*.\n\n    The result is the lowercased text with each run of characters that\n    are not ASCII letters or digits replaced by one ``-``, with leading\n    and trailing ``-`` removed.  Text with no ASCII letters or digits\n    yields an empty string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9]+\", \"-\", text.lower()).strip(\"-\")\n```\n\nRequirements traced to the implementation:\n\n1. **Lowercase** — `text.lower()`.\n2. **Runs of non-`[A-Za-z0-9]` become one `-`** — `re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9]+\", \"-\", ...)`.\n3. **Strip leading/trailing `-`** — `.strip(\"-\")`.\n4. **Empty for no letters/digits** — `\"---\"` → `\"-\"` → `\"\"`.\n\nExamples:\n- `slugify(\"Hello, World!\")` → `\"hello-world\"`\n- `slugify(\"  Multiple   Spaces  \")` → `\"multiple-spaces\"`\n\nOne caveat worth flagging honestly: this environment's command policy blocked all `run_command` invocations (including the suggested `unittest discover` command), so I could not execute the existing suite. I instead read the file back to confirm its final contents and manually traced each specified behavior, plus edge cases (`\"\"`, digits, underscores, non-ASCII text). If the suite can be run in an unrestricted shell, `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests` should exercise it.",
